/-! # BlowupB.Star — step 2 of the reduction: canonical spokes ↦ representative edges

At a vertex `x` of class `i`, the canonical spokes `∑ k, d k • cs x k` whose coefficient vector
`d` lies in the lattice generated by the type degree vectors `typeDegVec τ i` (`τ ∈ F`, `i ∈ τ`)
are rewritten, modulo copies, as edges among representatives:

* `star_type`: for one type `τ = {i, k, k'}`, `cs x k + cs x k' ≡ -(canon k x, canon k' x)`
  (cost `1`), and for `τ = {i, k, k}`, `2 • cs x k ≡ (rep–rep edges)` (cost `3`);
* `star_vertex`: linear combination over `τ`;
* `step2`: all vertices at once, from integral divisibility.
-/
